// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.closure [Closure-Form-Borrow]; rule.mem.read [Read]; CHG-0305; conf.closure-ref-capture-blocks-deref
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// The closure writes through the reference `r`, so it captures `r` itself by
// an exclusive borrow (spec/15 §6: the write's place root is `r`). `*r` in
// `main` reads `r`, and that read meets the closure's borrow. The closure
// row marks `r` escaped (D-0243), and since D-0288 the closure also holds
// `*r` exclusively, so the read is rejected before the run; until then it
// was checked when the program ran. coby read the reference without
// `[Read]`'s check until CHG-0305; cobc always faulted here.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto c = [r]() { *r = *r + 1; };
    *r = *r + 1;
    printf("%v\n", 0);
}
